  P-256/SHA-256 vectors are used as known-answer tests. Copyright (c) 2013 IETF Trust and the persons
  identified as the document authors.
- NIST FIPS 186-4, Digital Signature Standard (DSS), DOI 10.6028/NIST.FIPS.186-4: P-256 domain
  parameters. These were cross-checked against OpenSSL's explicit prime256v1 output
  (tests/fixtures/openssl_p256_explicit.txt, generated by OpenSSL 3.0.2 on szl-vm2).
- DSSE (Dead Simple Signing Envelope) protocol and envelope v1.0.2, secure-systems-lab/dsse, commit
  b531b787bb3e5f0c3e1c19cee84da1c5d569b061. The specification is licensed under the Community
  Specification License 1.0. The PAE definition and the protocol.md test vector are used; no
  reference code is used.
- SZL A11oy szl_dsse.py (szl-holdings/a11oy, commit 9250b016e13c823fabf9feee941299d12ccc7956). It is
  SZL's own code and was read only to match its conventions; it is not copied.

